<title>USA: Integra Life says skin provides permanence.</title>
<headline>Integra Life says skin provides permanence.</headline>
<dateline>PLAINSBORO, N.J. 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Integra LifeSciences Corp said Wednesday that long-term results of the multicenter clinical trial for the company's Integra Artificial Skin show that the product provides permanent skin replacement after full thickness burn injury.</p>
<p>In the long-term study, patients were evaluated for periods from slightly less than one year to more than two years following healing or discharge from the hospital.</p>
<p>Integra Artificial Skin is made up primarily of collagen.</p>
